  {"i":3707,"keep":[4],"n":"甘い 'lenient, soft on someone' (子どもに甘い) is a common learner sense and fits the character unit."},
  {"i":3708,"keep":[2],"n":"お隣/隣の人 'next-door neighbour, the house next door' is basic N5 and is taught with the neighbourhood."},
  {"i":3727,"keep":[],"n":"The 'kind, warm-hearted' sense is normally written 温かい; with the 暖 kanji the word belongs to weather only."},
  {"i":3792,"keep":[3],"n":"普通 'local train' (普通列車, station announcements) is common and taught with trains and stations."},
  {"i":3797,"keep":[3],"n":"結構です 'no, thank you' is a core polite set phrase for declining offers."},
  {"i":3804,"keep":[2],"n":"お邪魔します/お邪魔しました are basic polite set phrases used when visiting someone's home."},
